Whether a string is a palindrome, which the program decides by reversing it and comparing the two. The output is 1 for a palindrome and 0 otherwise. Case matters, so Aba is not one.
The probe is two lists walked together: the comparison stops as soon as one runs out, and checks both are empty together.
---
---
(lam s
  (letrec rev (lam l (lam acc
        (if (? l) acc ((rev (tail l)) [(head l) acc]))))
    (letrec same (lam a (lam b
          (if (? a) (? b)
              (if (? b) 0
                  (if (= (head a) (head b)) ((same (tail a)) (tail b)) 0)))))
      ((same s) ((rev s) ~)))))
---
"" => 1 fuel 200000
"a" => 1 fuel 200000
"abba" => 1 fuel 200000
"abc" => 0 fuel 200000
"Aba" => 0 fuel 200000
"racecar" => 1 fuel 200000
"ab" => 0 fuel 200000
"noon" => 1 fuel 200000
